5,Trans-New-Guinea languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/trans-new-guinea-languages/,These languages are spoken in Papua New Guinea and in Indonesian Papua. Total number of speakers (estimate): 2 million according to Foley (2006) Classification: The Trans-New Guinea language group includes about 400 languages.,Gavak,Trans-New Guinea
6,Gavak language - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Dimir_language,"Gavak, also known as Bosiken and Dimir, is a Papuan language of Madang Province, Papua New Guinea. It is spoken in the Dimir River area.",Gavak,Trans-New Guinea
7,Adelbert Range,https://grokipedia.com/page/adelbert_range,"The Adelbert Range is situated within the New Guinea orogenic belt, a complex zone of deformation resulting from the oblique collision between the Australian and Pacific plates, which has driven ongoing tectonic activity since the late Oligocene.",Gavak,Trans-New Guinea
